WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:03.970
Our brothers and sisters
are in desperate need

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.139
of assistance to serve
the people.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.974
You are the help that's coming.

00:00:09.341 --> 00:00:11.177
♪ (SOMBER MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.177 line:0%
SPEAKER:<i> The Navajo Nation</i>

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:13.479 line:0%
<i> is the largest tribe
 in the United States.</i>

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.615
<i> Twenty-seven thousand
 square miles</i>

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.849
<i> that we have to patrol.</i>

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:20.553
An increase in criminal
activity has come upon us.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.654
Come out!

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.690
SPEAKER 2:<i> To offer
 the basic police services,</i>

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.525
<i> we would need 500 officers.</i>

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:27.327
<i> We have 180.</i>

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.662
SPEAKER 3:<i> Quite frankly,
 our lives are at stake.</i>

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.565
SPEAKER 4:<i> Class 57,
 what makes you different</i>

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.536
<i> from any other officer in
 this country,</i>

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.837
<i> is you are Navajos.</i>

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.940
SPEAKER 5:<i> In the Navajo Nation,
 everyone knows each other.</i>

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.143
<i> I am worried about
 my dad's side finding out.</i>

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.644
They hate cops.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.046
SPEAKER 6:<i> I'm scared for her,
 but I know</i>

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.548
<i> she can handle herself.</i>

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.282
SPEAKER 7:<i> They're leaving
 left and right,</i>

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:52.084
<i> and that's kind of got
 me worried.</i>

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:55.754
If you think you can handle it,
don't quit.

00:00:55.854 --> 00:00:58.191
SPEAKER 8:<i> I think it's dire.
 Some people aren't prepared</i>

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:01.327
<i> mentally, emotionally, to deal
 with it in the long run.</i>

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:04.029
-You're okay. Control.
-(MUMBLING)

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.799
SPEAKER 9:<i> I'm willing to put
 my life at risk.</i>

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:07.867
I'm pretty scared, though.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:11.171
I've tried to tell myself,
keep pushing forward.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.706
OFFICER:<i> Stay where you are!</i>

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.109
It's been a rough couple years.
We're ready to move forward.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.746
SPEAKER 10:<i> The success of
 the Navajo police academy</i>

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.750
could break or make the nation.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.152
OFFICER 2:
<i> Navajo police!</i>

